        "original_id": "30379da6-c5a5-5f26-ac98-7acf25c6c532",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Juniperus, Indigofera, Cunninghamites elegans\n- Plant families: Cupressaceae, Fabaceae\n- Places: James Wild Horse Trap\n- Concepts: conifers, flowering plants, wild horse traps\n\nFacts:\n- Juniperus is a genus of coniferous plants in the cypress family Cupressaceae.\n- Indigofera is a large genus of more than 750 species of flowering plants in the family Fabaceae.\n- James Wild Horse Trap was the location of a corral and fences used to capture wild horses, and those structures were built from dead Juniper trees.\n- Cunninghamites elegans is an extinct conifer species in the family Cupressaceae.",
